1
00:00:00,621 --> 00:00:02,250
Five accounts say buy.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:03,990
Is that five opinions?

3
00:00:04,126 --> 00:00:06,992
Or one opinion, copied four times?

4
00:00:07,457 --> 00:00:09,369
Most trading bots can't tell the

5
00:00:09,119 --> 00:00:10,001
difference.

6
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:11,547
They count the noise,

7
00:00:11,684 --> 00:00:13,493
act on it, and keep no

8
00:00:13,256 --> 00:00:14,343
record of why.

9
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,929
This is Hanko.

10
00:00:16,092 --> 00:00:17,746
A hanko is the seal you

11
00:00:17,496 --> 00:00:19,435
stamp in Japan to commit to

12
00:00:19,197 --> 00:00:20,027
something.

13
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:22,527
Every decision here is stamped before

14
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:23,636
the outcome is known.

15
00:00:24,077 --> 00:00:26,428
It reads public voices on Telegram,

16
00:00:26,603 --> 00:00:28,309
Bluesky and X.

17
00:00:28,446 --> 00:00:30,333
A repost, a forward,

18
00:00:30,495 --> 00:00:31,995
or a copy with an ad

19
00:00:31,758 --> 00:00:34,263
pasted on counts as one voice.

20
00:00:34,387 --> 00:00:35,345
Not two.

21
00:00:35,764 --> 00:00:37,071
Then it decides.

22
00:00:37,208 --> 00:00:39,404
Enter, pass, or admit it can't

23
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:39,816
tell.

24
00:00:39,965 --> 00:00:41,478
It sizes the position,

25
00:00:41,383 --> 00:00:43,669
and writes down in advance exactly

26
00:00:43,432 --> 00:00:44,880
what would prove it wrong.

27
00:00:45,324 --> 00:00:47,507
Every run is sealed and anchored

28
00:00:47,321 --> 00:00:48,705
in a Bitcoin block.

29
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,638
Change one byte, and the seal

30
00:00:50,388 --> 00:00:51,141
breaks.

31
00:00:51,264 --> 00:00:52,519
Anyone can check it,

32
00:00:52,463 --> 00:00:54,620
with no account and no key.

33
00:00:55,077 --> 00:00:57,106
Before it buys, it checks it

34
00:00:56,869 --> 00:00:57,750
can sell.

35
00:00:57,912 --> 00:01:00,198
Selling fifty thousand dollars of BONK

36
00:00:59,961 --> 00:01:01,861
costs under three percent,

37
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:03,317
from a real quote.

38
00:01:03,454 --> 00:01:05,959
The textbook formula said seven point

39
00:01:05,709 --> 00:01:06,474
six.

40
00:01:06,911 --> 00:01:08,797
So we broke it on purpose.

41
00:01:08,934 --> 00:01:10,125
Sources down.

42
00:01:10,234 --> 00:01:11,399
Rate limits.

43
00:01:11,563 --> 00:01:13,114
A planted instruction.

44
00:01:13,264 --> 00:01:14,789
Tampered evidence.

45
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:16,259
Nine failures.

46
00:01:16,369 --> 00:01:17,418
Nine held.

47
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:20,176
And it runs every three hours,

48
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:22,225
on its own, in public.

49
00:01:22,388 --> 00:01:24,957
Three days later, every call is

50
00:01:24,707 --> 00:01:26,864
graded against the conditions it set

51
00:01:26,627 --> 00:01:27,444
itself.

52
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:28,681
Hanko.

53
00:01:28,831 --> 00:01:30,112
Don't trust the call.

54
00:01:30,261 --> 00:01:31,413
Check the receipt.

